  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-icon-theme",
      "text": "English | [简体中文](README.zh.md)\n\nAutomatic, coherent, and user-customizable icons for DeepSeek Harness Settings and sidebar actions.\n\n_Screenshots use the Chinese locale; the plugin ships equivalent English labels._"
    },
    {
      "section": "Why this plugin",
      "text": "`dsh-icon-theme` discovers the live slot ledger, preserves trustworthy original icons, fills recognizable gaps with a small Fluent-style pack, and lets the user override every supported target. Version 0.3 uses DSH's official configuration forms and, where available, the official Settings icon slot."
    },
    {
      "section": "Why this plugin",
      "text": "- Discovers live winning `settings.section` and `sidebar.footer.action` contributions generically. Audited per-plugin records are used only when a sidebar is partially rendered and cannot be correlated by order.\n- Stores choices by stable key, such as `settings.section:market`, never by translated labels or DOM position.\n- Ships 50 curated Fluent UI 16 Regular glyphs, 70 official DSH UI glyphs, and the audited monochrome dsh-market glyph (121 total).\n- Uses no icon CDN, webfont, Iconify API, GitHub request, or package scanning at runtime.\n- Restores every host SVG and owned DOM marker on unload or hot reload.\n- Reports non-rendered contributions and non-icon cards instead of pretending they were changed.\n- Falls back to the Settings gear when a target has neither a trustworthy match nor an original icon."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```bash\ndsh plugin --profile web add dsh-icon-theme\n```\n\nRestart `dsh web`, then open **Settings → Icons**.\n\nTo install from a source checkout instead:\n\n```bash\ngit clone https://github.com/yzke/dsh-icon-theme.git\ncd dsh-icon-theme\nnpm ci\nnpm run build\n\nRequires Node.js **24.9+**. The `engines.dsh` and DSH peer range is deliberately limited to the tested versions: **`0.2.1-rc.5 || 0.2.2-alpha.3`**. Other prereleases are not implicitly supported. For DSH 0.1, keep `dsh-icon-theme@0.2.3`."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "| DSH version | Settings icons | Configuration |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `0.2.1-rc.5` (npm latest at release) | Reversible DOM adapter | Official `configForms` |\n| `0.2.2-alpha.3` (preview) | Official `settings.section.icon` slot | Official `configForms` |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "**Desktop:** install through the desktop application's Plugin Manager, or its own bundled `dsh` command while the application is fully quit. Desktop owns the reserved `desktop` profile; the npm CLI cannot manage that profile. The shared Web client and Host APIs are supported by this package, but native Windows/macOS Desktop installers have not been end-to-end qualified. See [official Desktop ownership](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/blob/dsh-v0.2.2-alpha.3/apps/desktop/README.md#installation-ownership)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Uninstall",
      "text": "```bash\ndsh plugin --profile web remove dsh-icon-theme\n```\n\nRestart `dsh web`. The plugin restores every host SVG and removes all owned DOM markers and styles on unload."
    },
    {
      "section": "Use",
      "text": "The page lists every discovered target, its stable key, its compatibility state, and the source of the current icon. Search by feature name, ID, or icon; filter Settings/sidebar/unrecognized/customized entries; choose a glyph; or restore one/all targets to automatic behavior.\n\nResolution is deterministic:"
    },
    {
      "section": "Use",
      "text": "1. User override.\n2. Audited, bundled plugin glyph.\n3. Trustworthy DSH/plugin original.\n4. Exact stable-ID preset.\n5. Unambiguous stable-ID inference.\n6. Existing host fallback, or Settings gear when no original exists.\n\nLocalized labels are display and search text only. They never decide a persisted mapping."
    },
    {
      "section": "Sidebar behavior",
      "text": "| State | Behavior |\n| --- | --- |\n| Rendered icon action | Changeable; the original is preserved by default. |\n| Registered but not rendered | Listed as “can preset”; the override applies when it appears. |\n| Non-icon card | Reported but deliberately left unchanged. |\n| Unknown or changed DOM | Left untouched unless a unique audited compatibility record exists. |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Sidebar behavior",
      "text": "The sidebar footer and rc.5 Settings adapters remain narrow and reversible. Alpha.3 Settings uses official icon contributions, preserves other providers, and releases its overrides on unload. New surfaces such as `sidebar.panellist` are outside this plugin's scope. See [the design note](docs/design.md)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Sidebar behavior",
      "text": "When `dsh-better-sidebar` is installed, its own Settings row icon is treated as a trusted original and preserved by default. It is replaced only when the user chooses `replace-generic` (or a manual override)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Ecosystem checks",
      "text": "Compatibility fixtures are pinned to real open-source registration excerpts, including `dsh-full-remote`, `dsh-context`, `dsh-openpencil`, `dsh-approve-for-me`, and `dsh-composer-polish`. They prove that an unknown Settings section is discovered generically, while contributions to unrelated surfaces are not misidentified. Details and pinned commits are in [ecosystem compatibility](docs/ecosystem-compatibility.md). The sidebar fallback fingerprints are also pinned to upstream revisions and may need periodic updates if those plugins change their DOM."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development and release gate",
      "text": "```bash\nnpm ci\nnpm run qa\nnpm run test:web\nnpm pack --dry-run\n\nFor the optional live-host smoke test:\n\n```bash\nDSH_E2E_URL='http://127.0.0.1:3184/?token=TEST_PROFILE_TOKEN' npm run test:web -- -t @real-dsh\n```\n\nThe full testing contract is documented in [TESTING.md](TESTING.md). Icon sources and licenses are recorded in [THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md](THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Privacy and security",
      "text": "Detection reads only DSH slot metadata and the two rendered UI surfaces. The plugin does not inspect user files or other plugins' bundles. Preferences use DSH's shared `configForms` service for the `dsh-icon-theme` Host entry. DSH owns authentication, revision checks, persistence, and reconnection for both Web and Desktop; the plugin has no private HTTP endpoint or browser-local preference copy.\n\nMIT licensed."
    }
  ],
